 {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "I'm currently sending VIO message using mavsdk::Mocap::set_vision_position_estimate(VisionPositionEstimate vision_position_estimate) and assigning values at mavsdk::Mocap::VisionPositionEstimate respectively. The question is, what should be the timestamp format for this message? At first I tried std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::microseconds>(std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now().time_since_epoch()).count();, however visual odometry latency values appeared to be incredibly high in log file. Also set ts value to 0, as said [here]( https://mavsdk.mavlink.io/v0.21.1/en/api_reference/classmavsdk_1_1_mocap.html) to use internal timestamp, however nothing really changed, the latency values are still enormous. Log: https://review.px4.io/plot_app?log=8aeba5db-124c-499a-9df3-4416a1aaf438\r\nMy guess is that the timestamp in FCU's system time (seems like since boot) should be applied", "closed_by": {"login": "OPyshkin", "id": 42379117, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQyMzc5MTE3", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42379117?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/OPyshkin", "html_url": "https://github.com/OPyshkin", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/OPyshkin/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/OPyshkin/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/OPyshkin/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/OPyshkin/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/OPyshkin/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/OPyshkin/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/OPyshkin/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/OPyshkin/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/OPyshkin/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "reactions": {"url": "https: